And I really liked the power of Marshall telling him that.
我非常喜欢马修对他说这番话时的那种力量感。

00:13:25.758 --> 00:13:26.700
And Ted took it.
而且泰德听进去了。

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:32.220
And a good friend, I think, does provide their like bumpers, you know, so you don't go so far.
我想，一个好朋友确实会提供像缓冲护栏一样的东西，你知道的，免得你走得太远。

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:39.407
Some of us are thinking about those moments where in life, we all, every now and again, we all need that moment, don't we?
我们有些人会想起生活中那些时刻，我们每个人，时不时地，都需要那么一个时刻，不是吗？

00:13:39.407 --> 00:13:54.077
In one way or another, we need a friend to say like, Hey, I'm seeing whatever it may be, it may not be this context at all, but do you have that friend in life who can actually really have the uncomfortable conversation with you if you're off track?
以这样或那样的方式，我们需要一个朋友说，嘿，我看到的是……不管具体是什么情况，可能完全不是这种语境，但在生活中，当你偏离轨道时，你有没有这样一个能真正跟你进行这种不舒服对话的朋友？

00:13:54.077 --> 00:14:11.692
