我们让所有人都踏上了一条新的轨迹，虽然是一条走下坡路的轨迹，在公寓里是字面意义上的，而在泰德的爱情生活中则是象征意义上的。

00:49:53.176 --> 00:49:57.537
But boy, then rising from the ashes that hung over next morning after St.
但是天呐，随后在圣帕特里克节过后的清晨，阴霾消散，浴火重生。

00:49:57.537 --> 00:50:04.526
Patrick's Day, and Ted walking out with a yellow umbrella was our way of saying, keep watching this TV show, America.
泰德拿着一把黄雨伞走出来，这就是我们在对美国观众说：继续看这部电视剧吧。

00:50:04.526 --> 00:50:05.780
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:50:05.780 --> 00:50:08.169
I know we've been gone for three months.
我知道我们离开三个月了。

00:50:08.889 --> 00:50:12.502
We're making the case that we're still a show you want to watch.
我们在证明我们仍然是一部你想看的剧。

00:50:12.502 --> 00:50:22.210
And I think when Ted walks off off of that yellow umbrella, I felt very confident launching into our nine episodes in 10 and a half weeks, which we will talk about shortly.
而且我觉得当泰德拿着那把黄雨伞走开时，我对在十个半星期里推出我们剩下的九集感到非常有信心，我们很快就会聊到这个。

00:50:22.210 --> 00:50:24.010
Yeah.
对。

00:50:24.010 --> 00:50:31.530
In the flashback, the butt dial version of Ted with the bouncer when he goes rock and roll and he does this.
在闪回中，那个按错键给泰德打语音信箱的版本的泰德，和保安在一起时，他开始摇滚，然后做了这个动作。

00:50:31.530 --> 00:50:33.409
Like weird karate, weird karate.
就像奇怪的空手道，奇怪的空手道。

00:50:33.409 --> 00:50:34.929
Was that fun or awkward?
这很有趣还是让人觉得尴尬？

00:50:34.929 --> 00:50:36.849
Cause you were very funny doing that.
因为你做这个动作的时候非常搞笑。

00:50:36.849 --> 00:50:38.690
But it was like- I think I remember liking it.
但感觉就像——我想我记得我挺喜欢的。

00:50:38.690 --> 00:50:39.690
It was funny.
挺搞笑的。

00:50:39.690 --> 00:50:42.010
I think I thought it was, it was fun.
我觉得挺有意思的，挺好玩的。

00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:46.130
Like you said, you enjoy sometimes playing the things you did not get to play as Ted.
就像你说的，你有时很享受去演那些你在演泰德时演不到的东西。

00:50:46.130 --> 00:50:49.090
Maybe just weird and a different energy here and you lean into it.
也许只是感觉怪异，带有一种不同的能量，而你顺应了这种感觉。

00:50:49.090 --> 00:50:50.050
It's a college Ted.
那是大学时期的泰德。

00:50:50.050 --> 00:50:53.570
Yeah, or drunk Ted is like a whole different personality.
对，或者说喝醉的泰德完全是另一种性格。

00:50:54.369 --> 00:50:57.570
You know, Jordana said something really interesting at the end of this episode.
你知道，乔丹娜在这集结尾时说了一件很有意思的事。

00:50:57.570 --> 00:51:02.730
She said, it's so nice that you played a character on TV who got to change.
她说，你在电视上扮演了一个有机会改变的角色，这真是太好了。

00:51:02.730 --> 00:51:04.110
Yeah.
对。

00:51:04.110 --> 00:51:04.949
Yeah.
对。

00:51:04.949 --> 00:51:07.309
You know, so many TV characters are static.
你知道，很多电视剧的角色都是一成不变的。

00:51:07.309 --> 00:51:11.469
It's kind of like the form demands that they be static.
这种形式似乎就要求他们必须一成不变。

00:51:11.469 --> 00:51:22.750
You guys really were interested in character dimensionality and growth and learning and kind of momentum of, you're watching a guy grow up and you allowed him to grow up.
你们真的很关注角色的多面性、成长、学习，以及那种推动力，你看着一个角色长大，而且你们允许他长大。

00:51:22.750 --> 00:51:24.590
And I always really appreciated that.
我一直非常感激这一点。

00:51:24.590 --> 00:51:31.789
And my daughter's obsessed with The Simpsons right now and there was just a joke on The Simpsons where they said, we're characters in the comedy, we never change.
我女儿现在迷上了《辛普森一家》，《辛普森一家》里刚好有个笑话，他们说：我们是喜剧里的角色，我们永远不会变。

00:51:31.789 --> 00:51:34.150
And they all laugh and it's like the last line of an episode.
然后他们都笑了，就像是一集的最后一句台词。

00:51:34.150 --> 00:51:37.420
But in this, like, this, Ted changes.
但在《老爸老妈浪漫史》里，泰德会改变。

00:51:37.420 --> 00:51:43.272
Ted changes and evolves and the end of this episode says, keep watching, you're going to like where Ted's going next from here.
泰德会改变和进化，这集的结尾仿佛在说：继续看下去吧，你会喜欢接下来泰德的走向的。

00:51:43.272 --> 00:51:47.143
This is a low point, but this is you're going to watch him rise like a Phoenix here.
这是一个低谷，但你会看着他在这里像凤凰涅槃一样崛起。

00:51:47.143 --> 00:51:58.479
And there's the energy at the end of this episode, I felt very excited watching the episode because it reminded me of like, we were saying challenge accepted, we had to do nine episodes intended to have weeks and we had been off for three months.
这集结尾的那种能量，我看着觉得非常兴奋，因为它让我想起，我们当时就像是在接受挑战，我们必须在十个半星期里拍完九集，而且我们已经停播了三个月。

00:51:58.479 --> 00:52:02.949
And we had, you know, we didn't know if people are going to keep watching, we're going to cancel.
而且我们，你知道，我们不知道观众还会不会继续看，我们会不会被砍。

00:52:02.949 --> 00:52:06.405
And we said like, bring it on, we're going to give you nine great episodes.
我们当时说，尽管放马过来吧，我们要奉献九集精彩的剧集。

00:52:06.405 --> 00:52:07.603
And I think we really did.
我觉得我们真的做到了。

00:52:07.603 --> 00:52:09.170
I think these back nine are great.
我觉得后九集非常棒。

00:52:09.170 --> 00:52:11.059
So I'm excited to watch the rest of them.
所以我很高兴能看剩下的部分。

00:52:16.159 --> 00:52:23.865
And we're back for a section we like to call C block, it's the C block.
我们回到了我们喜欢称之为C板块的环节，这就是C板块。

00:52:23.865 --> 00:52:32.440
We love to read letters from you, it sounds like a prison, an area of a prison.
我们喜欢读你们的来信，听起来像个监狱，监狱里的某个区域。

00:52:33.800 --> 00:52:35.480
I'm anist about the way we do this time.
我对我们这次做节目的方式感到有点不好意思。

00:52:36.199 --> 00:52:37.856
We love to hear from you.
我们喜欢听你们分享。

00:52:37.856 --> 00:52:41.833
As you know, we, we open the show with voice notes from you.
如你所知，我们用你们的语音留言开启节目。

00:52:41.833 --> 00:52:44.550
We close the show with a letter from you.
我们用你们的来信结束节目。

00:52:44.550 --> 00:52:47.665
Let us know how this podcast is landing on you.
让我们知道这个播客对你们有什么影响。

00:52:47.665 --> 00:52:58.599
If you're enjoying your rewatch and re-listen with us, let us know about your relationship to how I made your mother go to how we made your mother.com, HWMYM, HWMYM.
如果你喜欢和我们一起重温和重听，请让我们知道你与《老爸老妈浪漫史》的缘分，访问 howwemadyourmother.com，HWMYM，HWMYM。

00:52:58.599 --> 00:53:01.623
Go to contact, follow the directions.
点击联系，按照指示操作。

00:53:01.623 --> 00:53:02.604
Very simple.
非常简单。

00:53:02.604 --> 00:53:09.960
We have a letter today from, I believe, Harrison from the Pacific Northwest, from Seattle.
我们今天收到了一封信，我想发信人是来自太平洋西北地区西雅图的哈里森。

00:53:09.960 --> 00:53:14.159
In 2013, I was in a pretty toxic college relationship.
2013年时，我正处一段相当有毒的大学恋爱关系中。

00:53:14.159 --> 00:53:19.039
I was self-centered and treated everyone else like an extra in a movie about my life.
我以自我为中心，把其他人当成我人生电影里的群众演员。

00:53:19.039 --> 00:53:21.320
You were just saying that, that's crazy.
你刚才正这么说呢，太疯狂了。

00:53:21.320 --> 00:53:25.599
Unsurprisingly, I drove all my friends and eventually girlfriend away.
不出所料，我把所有的朋友甚至是后来的女朋友都气走了。

00:53:25.599 --> 00:53:29.000
Depressed, I flipped on the pilot of how I met your mother.
我陷入抑郁，打开了《老爸老妈浪漫史》的试播集。

00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:38.360
For the next several weeks, I escaped into this increasingly warm place of hopefulness, love, and more importantly, the friends I no longer had and really needed.
在接下来的好几个星期里，我逃进了一个充满希望、爱意，更重要的是充满了我不再拥有却极度需要的友谊的温馨世界里。

00:53:38.360 --> 00:53:44.400
About halfway through the run of the show, I found those friends by chance in the back of a carpool to an event I was working.
在大约播出一半的时候，我在我参加的一个活动的车后座上偶然找到了这些朋友。

00:53:44.400 --> 00:53:48.480
One invited me to play pond hockey like a week later, and we were fast friends.
大概一周后，其中一个人邀请我去打冰球，我们很快成了好朋友。

00:53:48.480 --> 00:53:55.920
These guys are loving and honest enough to tell me what I needed to hear about my choices in life, and they weren't, and still aren't shy about it.
这群家伙很有爱心，也很诚实，敢于把我对生活选择的真实看法告诉我，而且他们过去和现在对此都毫不避讳。

00:53:55.920 --> 00:54:03.963
All along, I was burying the Ted that I thought I was beneath a thick layer of the objectionable qualities of Barney.
一直以来，我都把自以为是的那个泰德埋在了巴尼那些令人反感的特质的厚厚外表之下。

00:54:03.963 --> 00:54:04.463
Wow.
哇。

00:54:04.463 --> 00:54:07.969
I wanted to find the right girl, but I didn't know.
我想找到对的女孩子，但我并不懂。

00:54:07.969 --> 00:54:09.344
I just wasn't ready.
我只是还没准备好。

00:54:09.119 --> 00:54:09.619
The St.
圣帕特里克节那一集，

00:54:09.619 --> 00:54:12.842
Patrick's Day episode, No Tomorrow, slapped me in the face.
《没有明天》，狠狠地扇了我一巴掌。

00:54:12.842 --> 00:54:14.753
It opened my eyes to what it meant.
它让我睁开眼看清了这意味着什么。

00:54:14.753 --> 00:54:18.139
Do not be ready to meet my person and what an ass I was being.
我根本没准备好去遇到那个对的人，而我之前是多么像个混蛋。

00:54:18.139 --> 00:54:23.437
Eventually, the show taught me to be vulnerable enough to be honest with myself and make changes.
最终，这部剧教会我要有足够的脆弱来对自己诚实并做出改变。

00:54:23.320 --> 00:54:25.570
It made me believe in things again.
它让我重新开始相信事物。

00:54:25.570 --> 00:54:29.621
It empowered me to face my suicidal demons and shout them down.
它赋予我力量去面对我内心的自杀恶魔并大声斥退它们。

00:54:29.621 --> 00:54:38.430
However much pain I faced going forward, I suddenly had this very real light of belief in me that I was going to go where I needed to go.
无论未来我要面对多少痛苦，我的内心突然有了一束非常真实的信仰之光，指引我走向我该去的地方。

00:54:38.430 --> 00:54:41.645
My ladder was just propped against the wrong wall.
我只是把梯子靠错了墙。

00:54:41.645 --> 00:54:42.545
Today, I'm 31.
如今，我31岁了。

00:54:42.545 --> 00:54:49.875
I'm married going on three years to a woman I would never have deserved and frankly wasn't ready for 12 years ago.
我和一个我12年前绝不配拥有、坦白讲也还没准备好面对的女性结婚快三年了。

00:54:49.875 --> 00:54:54.311
In your work, I learned to love myself enough to give love to others.
在你们的作品中，我学会了爱自己，从而能够去爱别人。

00:54:54.311 --> 00:54:58.619
It taught me to value, cherish and fiercely protect my friendships.
它教会我珍视、珍惜并拼死守护我的友谊。

00:54:58.619 --> 00:54:59.460
P.S.
P.S.

00:54:59.460 --> 00:55:01.820
Thank you for the killer soundtrack to the show.
谢谢你为节目制作了这么棒的配乐。

00:55:01.820 --> 00:55:06.440
No show has ever done better.
没有任何节目能做得比这更好了。

00:55:06.440 --> 00:55:08.440
That's music to your ears, Craig.
克雷格，这听起来真是太悦耳了。

00:55:08.440 --> 00:55:09.679
Oh my God.
哦，天哪。

00:55:09.679 --> 00:55:15.960
To all our ears, Josh Radner is responsible for a few wonderful picks in that playlist.
对我们所有人来说，乔什·拉德纳对播放列表里一些精彩曲目的挑选功不可没。

00:55:15.960 --> 00:55:24.760
Thank you for that letter and for that level of honesty, of sharing that whole journey that's so on theme for this episode, it's exactly what we just spent this whole episode talking about.
谢谢你的来信，感谢你展现出的那份坦诚，分享了你走过的整段心路历程，这和我们这期节目的主题简直完美契合，这正是我们刚刚花了一整期节目在讨论的内容。

00:55:24.760 --> 00:55:30.400
And it's just real, it's human, we've all been there in one way or another at one time or another.
而且这很真实，很有人情味，我们都在某个时期、以这样或那样的方式经历过这一切。

00:55:30.400 --> 00:55:31.239
Sometimes you were many times.
有时你甚至经历过很多次。

00:55:31.239 --> 00:55:33.239
God, you were such a dick back in the day, Craig.
天哪，克雷格，你以前真是个混蛋。

00:55:33.239 --> 00:55:34.639
I've been a dick plenty of times.
我以前确实当过很多次混蛋。

00:55:34.639 --> 00:55:44.519
I've been, or whatever it is, whatever way you're lost and to someone tell you, to someone help you or to someone just like walk away because it seems too complicated.
不管是哪种迷失，不管是以什么方式迷失，然后有人来指点你、帮助你，或者只是因为觉得太复杂而选择走开。

00:55:44.519 --> 00:55:45.519
We've all been there.
我们都经历过。

00:55:45.519 --> 00:55:47.159
I really appreciate the honesty of now.
我真的很感激这种当下流露的坦诚。

00:55:47.159 --> 00:55:50.639
It's also funny how the show itself was his Marshall.
也有趣的是，节目本身就是他的“马歇尔”。

00:55:50.639 --> 00:55:52.199
Yes, the show is his Marshall.
没错，节目就是他的马歇尔。

00:55:52.199 --> 00:55:54.800
The show sat him down and said, Hey, check this out.
节目让他坐下来，然后说，嘿，来看看这个。

00:55:54.800 --> 00:55:58.039
And that's just amazing.
这实在是太神奇了。

00:55:58.039 --> 00:56:00.039
That's just such a gift to hear stories like that.
听到这样的故事真是一份厚礼。

00:56:00.039 --> 00:56:08.079
It's also like, I not to quote myself, but in Happy Thinking More, please, I have that line, every five years you realize what an asshole you were five years ago.
而且，就像——我可不是在引经据典，但在《Happy Thinking More, please》里我有这么一句：每隔五年，你就会意识到五年前的自己是个多大的白痴。

00:56:08.079 --> 00:56:08.920
Yes.
对的。

00:56:08.920 --> 00:56:18.800
And I think that like, if you're growing, if you're doing the thing and growing us, you will look back on your former self with some measure of embarrassment.
我觉得，如果你在成长，如果你在不断进步，你回首过去的自己时，多少会感到有些尴尬。

00:56:18.800 --> 00:56:19.920
Yes.
没错。

00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:22.719
You just will, like it's inevitable.
你就是会这样，因为这是不可避免的。

00:56:22.719 --> 00:56:24.199
Because it's evolution, right?
因为这就是进化，对吧？

00:56:24.199 --> 00:56:33.159
I mean, it's like, yeah, it's like every, Like, think about everything just feels modern until you see pictures of yourself 20 years ago.
我的意思是，就像，每件事——比如，你觉得一切都很时髦，直到你看到自己20年前的照片。

00:56:33.159 --> 00:56:35.079
And you're like, we were wearing what?
然后你会想：我们当年穿的都是些什么啊？

00:56:35.079 --> 00:56:36.679
Every time, you know?
每次都这样，你知道吗？

00:56:36.679 --> 00:56:39.599
Yes, every time.
对，每次都这样。

00:56:39.599 --> 00:56:44.679
But we have to be generous and we have to be sympathetic to ourselves.
但我们必须宽容，我们必须对自己多一点同理心。

00:56:44.679 --> 00:56:51.760
And I think that Harrison from Seattle was just generous enough to say I wasn't ready to meet my wife.
我觉得来自西雅图的哈里森足够坦然，他说自己当时还没准备好遇到他的妻子。

00:56:51.760 --> 00:56:55.760
And now I'm lucky enough to have met her at the right time.
而现在我很幸运能在对的时间遇到了她。

00:56:55.760 --> 00:57:06.019
I think that that's, you know, you consider on wallowing and hating your past self, or you can thank him for being a step along the way.
我觉得，你知道的，你可以选择沉溺于自责并痛恨过去的自己，或者你可以感谢他作为你成长路上的一个台阶。

00:57:06.019 --> 00:57:08.119
He made those mistakes to get you somewhere.
他犯下的那些错误，是为了带你走到今天的位子。

00:57:08.119 --> 00:57:09.340
Yeah.
是的。

00:57:09.340 --> 00:57:11.920
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:57:11.920 --> 00:57:13.920
Please equip me.
请赐予我救赎吧。

00:57:13.920 --> 00:57:15.920
All sins are forgiven.
所有的罪过都已被原谅。

